config FIBRIL_CAN_NODE_ADC_PORT
	bool
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_FIBRIL_FCAN_ADC_PORT_ENABLED
	imply ADC
	imply MOTOR
	help
	  Compiled whenever the devicetree lists calibration inputs under a
	  fibril,fcan-adc-port node, which is also what puts AdcPort instances
	  into the schema. MdMotor's calibration reads its inputs through this;
	  without it, sensor_state answers that the node has no ports.

	  ADC and MOTOR are implied rather than selected: a port list made of
	  only one kind needs only that subsystem, and the build of the other
	  kind fails loudly if it is turned off.

config FIBRIL_CAN_NODE_ADC_PORT_MAX
	int "AdcPort instances to allocate for"
	default 16
	range 1 32
	depends on FIBRIL_CAN_NODE_ADC_PORT
	help
	  The schema's max_count for AdcPort: how many instances the generated
	  code reserves state for. It is a ceiling, not a count, and never
	  reaches the schema blob.

	  16 covers CanMotorMbed's miniv4 layout of 13 ports. Lowering it below
	  the devicetree's child count fails the BUILD_ASSERT in adc_port.cpp.
